{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1466983-spoiler-alert-for-the-3-alpha-templates-created-from-the-hammersmith-event","id":1466983,"title":"Spoiler alert for the 3 alpha templates created from the Hammersmith Event","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-06T13:34:46-07:00","id":1466983,"title":"Spoiler alert for the 3 alpha templates created from the Hammersmith Event","content":"So Max Mercer, Sara Kaur and Michael Donighal became unusually powerful examples of their types from the Hammersmith Event, but did they need to be? Well, Max needs to be unique in his ability to travel through time, so he does need to be an anomaly, but I think it would be more interesting if Donighal and Kaur started off with PC power levels and rules and just got so powerful because they lived for so long. Like maybe they got some special properties, but otherwise immediately after the Hammersmith Event you could have built both of them as a starting Nova and a starting Psiad respectfully. I believe that both Nova's and Psiad's can gain access to enhanced lifespan fairly easily, so that part of their history doesn't need to be attributed to them being super special variants of their types. <br /> <br /> So how powerful are they supposed to be? I believe in the original Adventure! the narrative implied that Donighal was an actual Nova while everyone else were the less powerful Stalwart quantum using variant. He was someone notable for the time, but not necessarily someone notable if he had appeared in the Nova Age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T16:54:58-07:00","id":1466997,"title":"","content":"Divis Mal may be a very broadly powerful figure, but a lot of Nova Age characters seem to greatly outshine him in their own way. As one example, although he was an up-and-coming scientist before the Hammersmith Event, and became the self proclaimed smartest man in the world afterwards, the only notable super science device he made appears to be the one that started the Nova Age, and that took him nearly a century to build (although he was hampered by the Doyen Barrier). There were Nova Age scientists who seem to have cured a new disease every few weeks, or revolutionized some other field with similar frequency.<br /> <br /> In game terms, I suspect he had a few dots of Mega-Intellect and zero Mega Edges related to inventing. He never pushed harder in that direction because he was more interested in investigating <i>his</i> potential than building trinkets to uplift the world. Most Nova Age inventors would probably crush him in their field of expertise. In other words, he was the smartest man in the world when he was the only Mega-Intellect nova, but that changed.<br /> <br /> In the end, he was so powerful because he had a century long head start, no nova competition, and the Chrysalis Edge to give him the exact powers he wanted.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T17:51:19-07:00","id":1467003,"title":"","content":"I don't think we have anything that says Sara or Michael were unusually powerful in a larger context, only compared to their peers. Michael was more powerful than most stalwarts, and Sara was more powerful than most mesmerists. So, effectively, Michael was a nova among stalwarts, and Sara was a psiad among mesmerists.<br /> <br /> Max was unusually powerful both compared to other daredevils, and also from that larger context, due to the nature of how Talent Inspiration works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T18:54:25-07:00","id":1467006,"title":"","content":"Divis Mal is the most powerful Nova in Nova Age. Yes, of course there are Novas that can do things he can\u2019t, but he has mastered his own powers and can reach scale of power no one can during the time. Sure, it\u2019s due his age, but he worked hard to get there, his jumpstart was not a full eruption (he didn\u2019t get 150 experience to spend in powers, in rule terms), like the ones Novas got in later years, he was the ultimate Stalwart, but far from what a Novas could reach 100 years later.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would put stalwarts as Quantum 1 Novas, with the most powerful Stalwarts capable of maxing out to reach quantum 2. Mal would be a Quantum 2 Nova, capable of do routinely what others could do by doing their their best and with some luck. That\u2019s not a big deal on Nova era, but not much is a big deal in Nova era.<br /> <br /> Same for a Mesmerist, Sarah would be a Psi 4 Psiad when most psiads are caped in Psi 3. And Max is a Inspiration 15 Talent, or whatever you call what Max is, while other talents are caped in 10.<br /> <br /> Now, Primoris was extremely mental, while amazingly powerful, he hide his physical power to show how powerful his mind is. He is a sxientist and was mainly concerned with inventing things to Aeon society. His studies of the nature of telluric energy and the nature of Stalwarts, Mesmerists and Daredevils was fundamental for the later study of Novas and Psiads and Psions in the later eras, not to mention he invented chrysalis, what is not something to ignore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}